                    872.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. Workman’s compensation procedures fall directly under Department of Labor (DOL). Refer to current Department of Labor website for processes and procedures or contact the Injury Compensation Program Administrator (ICPA) located in the Human Resource Office.",
            "block_bbox": [
                131,
                903,
                1079,
                1015
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    131.0,
                    903.0
                ],
                [
                    1079.0,
                    903.0
                ],
                [
                    1079.0,
                    1015.0
                ],
                [
                    131.0,
                    1015.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "2. It is the Employer's responsibility to advise, orient and assist Employees regarding entitlement to medical and loss-of-pay benefits for injuries or illnesses that occur which are job related. The injured Employee's Supervisor will ensure the Employee understands his or her rights and options under the Federal Employee's Compensation Act.",
            "block_bbox": [
                129,
                1041,
                1070,
                1182
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    129.0,
                    1041.0
                ],
                [
                    1070.0,
                    1041.0
                ],
                [
                    1070.0,
                    1182.0
                ],
                [
                    129.0,
                    1182.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "3. It is the Employee's responsibility to report any injury or illness that he or she feels may be job related to the Supervisor immediately after the occurrence. Any representation will be IAW 20 CFR Part 10.701.",
            "block_bbox": [
                130,
                1207,
                1051,
                1294
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 11,
            "group_id": 10,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    130.0,
                    1207.0
                ],
                [
                    1051.0,
                    1207.0
                ],
                [
                    1051.0,
                    1294.0
                ],
                [
                    130.0,
                    1294.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "4. When the Employee is incapacitated and unable to notify the Supervisor of injury or illness, it shall be Management's responsibility to initiate the required procedures as soon as they are aware an incident has occurred.",
